{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel shall make the Passover.</b> In addition to what they did on the eighth day for the ordination and the dedication of the princes, they shall also make the Passover, so that they not exempt themselves from it on account of the joy of the commandments they had already fulfilled — as happened with the building of the First Temple, when our Sages of blessed memory (Mo'ed Katan 9a) recounted that Solomon suspended Yom Kippur because of the joy of the Temple's dedication."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:04.813751180Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}